# Build context exclusions for BOTH Dockerfile.builder and Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Both Dockerfiles do `COPY . .`, and the build context is this directory
# (scripts/14-builder-build.sh passes "${src}"). Without this file the builder image absorbs
# whatever build output happens to be lying in the working tree -- so the image content depends on
# what the developer last ran, and two developers produce different images from the same commit.
# That is non-determinism baked into an air-gap artifact every cluster node must pull.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-25 on a working tree: 438 MB of UNTRACKED local build output across the six apps
# (rust target/ 346 MB, dotnet tests/bin 50 MB, java target/ 23 MB, the go binary 15 MB, nodejs
# node_modules 4.3 MB). None of it is tracked -- `git ls-files` over apps/ returns zero bin/obj/
# target/node_modules entries -- so a clean CI checkout never sees it and the bloat is invisible
# there. Two tells that it was COPIED rather than built: the go builder compiles to /dev/null yet
# shipped a 15 MB binary, and the dotnet builder's last RUN is only `dotnet restore` yet shipped
# 50 MB of tests/bin.
#
# Dependency CACHES are deliberately NOT excluded here -- they live outside the context anyway
# ($CARGO_HOME, ~/.m2, /root/.nuget, the npm cache), which is what makes the offline build work.

# --- build output for this app ---
bin/
obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- never useful in an image ---
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp
